 "research": "Proven 30 deg incline bench body. Start = the approved incline neutral-grip press start (elev 45, plane -30, forearm vertical): bar ~4 cm above the upper chest. A Smith bar runs on fixed rails, so the top is set straight above the start: with the torso ~62 deg back from vertical the start hand sits ~0.13 m toward the feet of the shoulder, so the end arm points 106 deg / plane 88 (not 118, which would end over the face). The rails are drawn through the bar's real start and end positions; the stills log prints their tilt (must be under 8 deg). Grip slightly wider than the shoulders (hands ~0.43 m from the midline). Schick 2010 (Smith vs free bench), Lauver 2016 (30-45 deg incline).",
